      "id": "alignas",
      "name": "alignas",
      "category": "TransformNonVectorized",
      "signature": "alignas(T)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "T",
          "type": "alignof ( TQuat<"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<T> struct",
      "docs": "Transform composed of Scale, Rotation (as a quaternion), and Translation.\nTransforms can be used to convert from one space to another, for example by transforming\npositions and directions from local space to world space.\nTransformation of position vectors is applied in the order:  Scale -> Rotate -> Translate.\nTransformation of direction vectors is applied in the order: Scale -> Rotate.\nOrder matters when composing transforms: C = A * B will yield a transform C that logically\nfirst applies A then B to any subsequent transformation. Note that this is the opposite order of quaternion (TQuat<T>) multiplication.\nExample: LocalToWorld = (DeltaRotation * LocalToWorld) will change rotation in local space by DeltaRotation.\nExample: LocalToWorld = (LocalToWorld * DeltaRotation) will change rotation in world space by DeltaRotation."
    },
